From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: durunduk <drebdebian@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 12:10:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] tu: Align allocations of 64 KiB and more to 64 KiB

D3D12 guarantees 64 KiB aligned GPU virtual addresses and UE5 relies on
it. kgsl only page-aligns by default and the WinNative Vulkan wrapper
does not forward VK_VALVE_buffer_device_address_allocation_alignment, so
vkd3d-proton gets 4-8 KiB aligned heaps ("Requested alignment of 10000,
but got GPU VA of ... which is not aligned as expected") while UE 5.6
(Styx: Blades of Greed, Adreno 840) renders shattered geometry. The
misalignment is the suspected cause.

Default every allocation of at least 64 KiB to 64 KiB alignment, as
desktop drivers effectively do. TU_ALIGN_64K=0 restores the old
behaviour.
---
diff --git a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_device.cc b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_device.cc
index 4f15084..6a24885 100644
--- a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_device.cc
+++ b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_device.cc
@@ -3746,6 +3746,20 @@ tu_AllocateMemory(VkDevice _device,
                            BUFFER_DEVICE_ADDRESS_ALIGNMENT_ALLOCATE_INFO_VALVE);
    uint64_t alignment = align_info ? align_info->alignment : 0;
 
+   /* D3D12 guarantees 64 KiB aligned GPU addresses for heaps and buffers and
+    * UE5 relies on it (vkd3d-proton: "UE5 relies on GPUVAs to be aligned to
+    * the heap alignment"). kgsl only page-aligns by default, so allocations
+    * through translation layers that do not request an alignment (the
+    * WinNative Vulkan wrapper does not know VK_VALVE_buffer_device_address_
+    * allocation_alignment) get 4-8 KiB aligned addresses, suspected to
+    * shatter UE5 geometry. Desktop drivers align large allocations anyway.
+    * TU_ALIGN_64K=0 restores the old behaviour.
+    */
+   if (alignment < (1ull << 16) &&
+       pAllocateInfo->allocationSize >= (1ull << 16) &&
+       debug_get_bool_option("TU_ALIGN_64K", true))
+      alignment = 1ull << 16;
+
    if (fd_info && fd_info->handleType) {
       assert(fd_info->handleType ==
                 VK_EXTERNAL_MEMORY_HANDLE_TYPE_OPAQUE_FD_BIT ||
